{"name": "propose_test", "arguments": {"name": "Outdoor vs Construction Consumer Test", "theories": ["T1", "T2"], "method": "Online survey with simulated purchase intent. Recruit 500 participants: 250 outdoor enthusiasts (hiking, cycling, camping) and 250 construction workers (professional trades, DIY). Randomly assign each participant to one of two product versions: (A) a differentiated outdoor safety helmet with advanced impact protection and Bluetooth connectivity; (B) a differentiated construction safety hard hat with advanced impact protection and compliance certification. Participants view the product",
"sample": "500 participants (250 outdoor enthusiasts, 250 construction workers)", "measure": "Willingness to pay (WTP) measured on a 7-point scale (1=Would not pay at all to 7=Would pay a lot more). Also ask: \"How likely are you to purchase this product?\" (1=Very unlikely to 7=Very likely).", "prediction_by_theory": {"T1": "Outdoor enthusiasts will show a WTP at least 20% higher than construction workers for the outdoor helmet, and a purchase likelihood score at least 15% higher.", "T2": "Construction workers will show a WTP at least 15% higher than outdoor enthusiasts for the construction helmet, and a purchase likelihood score at least 10% higher."}, "decision_rule": "If the average WTP for the outdoor helmet is at least 20% higher than the construction helmet, we conclude T1 is more likely. If the average WTP for the construction helmet is at least 15% higher, we conclude T2 is more likely. If the difference is less than 15%",
"cost_eur": 18000, "weeks": 10}}
